---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
const email = site.supportEmail;
---

<Legal title="Terms of Service" description={`The rules for playing ${site.gameName} and using this website.`}>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {site.studioName} (“we”, “us”) about {site.gameName} (the “game”)
    and this website (together, the “service”). By playing the game or using the website you accept them. If you
    don’t agree, please don’t use the service.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who can play</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least {site.minimumAge} years old, or older where your country requires it. If you are under 18 (or
    the age of majority where you live), a parent or guardian must agree to these terms and should supervise any purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The game creates an account for you automatically. Linking an email and password in the game’s settings keeps your progress safe and lets you sign in on this website.</li>
    <li>Keep your password private. You are responsible for what happens on your account.</li>
    <li>One person, one account. Don’t sell, share or transfer accounts.</li>
    <li>You can ask us to delete your account at any time on the <a href="/delete-account/">account deletion page</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Gems, coins and other virtual items</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Gems, coins, heroes, pets, skins, crates and other in-game items are a limited, personal licence to use content in the game. You don’t own them, and they have no real-world money value.</li>
    <li>They can’t be exchanged for money, sold or traded outside the game.</li>
    <li>We may change or rebalance items and prices as the game evolves. We won’t remove paid items you already collected without a good reason (for example a refund, a chargeback or cheating).</li>
    <li>Items are lost if your account is deleted or suspended for breaking these terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Purchases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>In the app, purchases go through Google Play (or the App Store) under their terms.</li>
    <li>On this website, payments are handled by our payment provider; we never see your full card details. The price is the one shown at checkout, including tax where required.</li>
    <li>Web purchases are delivered to your in-game inbox. Open the game while online and claim them there.</li>
    <li>Refunds are covered by our <a href="/refunds/">Refund Policy</a> and your legal rights as a consumer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Redeem codes</h2>
  <p>
    Codes can be redeemed once per account, may expire or have limited uses, and have no cash value. Codes may not
    be sold. We may cancel codes that were obtained or used improperly, and we limit how often codes can be tried.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Fair play</h2>
  <p>Please don’t:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>cheat, edit your save data, use modified versions of the game, bots or exploits;</li>
    <li>interfere with the service, our servers or other players’ experience;</li>
    <li>use offensive, hateful or impersonating names, or build offensive public villages;</li>
    <li>abuse refunds or chargebacks.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may remove content, reset scores, rename you, hide your public village or leaderboard entry, or suspend or close
    accounts that break these rules. If you think we made a mistake, contact us.
  </p>

  <h2>7. What other players can see</h2>
  <p>
    Your display name, leaderboard scores and public village (buildings, decorations, heroes and similar) are visible
    to other players. Don’t put personal information in your name.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes and availability</h2>
  <p>
    We keep improving the game, which means features, events and content change. We try to keep the service running,
    but it may sometimes be unavailable. If we ever close the game, we will give notice in the game.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided “as is”. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect losses or for losses
    of virtual items. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law that can’t be waived.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. For important changes we’ll tell you in the game or on this website before they apply.
    Continuing to use the service after that means you accept the new terms.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
